pt09 adversarial lane, surface: gate morphology inflections. Greens the RED
frozen in the previous commit. Third and last known copy of the defect shape
v2.6.14 and 959d32c each fixed once elsewhere: an inflection list that names
some forms of a verb and misses the rest.

  dat(?:e|es|ing) (?:across|up|down)  ->  dat(?:e|es|ed|ing) …
  marry(?:ing)?   (?:up|down)         ->  marr(?:y|ies|ied|ying) …

Named forms rather than a stem, on v2.6.14's precedent: `marr\w*` is shorter
and admits "marred". The frame's second requirement — an ordinary relational
noun beside the idiom — is untouched, so no calendar sense can reach this:
"the invoice was dated up to the last quarter" and "the paint was marred up
near the ceiling" both stay binned, and the test pins both.

Measured:
- frozen gate benchmark IDENTICAL — 191 cases, domainRecall 1.0000,
  ignorePrecision 1.0000, junkRecall 0.8529, every verdict and reason code
  byte-for-byte the same before and after. The widening is free on all 191.
- corpus stance census IDENTICAL — 0 of 1,298 matches move, and the zero is
  attributed rather than assumed: `dated up`, `married up` and `marries up`
  occur zero times across all 42 archived sources. No score moves, so there is
  no threshold crossing to rule.
- the residual, named: a passage whose only relational evidence is `dated`
  itself still bins ("She dated up and he settled."). Fixing that means
  widening the co-requirement to bare `dated`, which buys the calendar false
  positives 959d32c refused, so it is recorded rather than shipped.

All 18 suite steps green.

